一.Advantages
1.Strong global optimization ability and not easy to fall into local optima
2.Extremely wide range of applications with no strict function constraints
3.Simple logic, easy to implement and few parameters
4.Good robustness and insensitive to initial values

二.Disadvantages
1.Slow convergence speed and computational high cost
2.Sensitive to parameters and parameter tuning depends on experience
3.Search efficiency drops sharply for high - dimensional problems
4.Insufficient convergence accuracy in the later stage
5.Not naturally friendly to parallel computing
